ATX4VC lets you **use ATX power supply on vintage computers**.

* Plug in ATX PSU on one end

* Get +12V, +5V, +3.3V, -5V, -12V out the other!

![enter image description here](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dekuNukem/ATX4VC/master/photos/title2.jpeg "enter image title here")

* Universal Voltage with Fused Rails

* Toolless Terminal Block

* PC Fan Header

* Fan speed, soft power, ARGB animation, temperature sensor with optional MCU board.

You can use ATX4VC to:

* Replace retro computer PSUs

* Test and diagnose vintage hardware

* As a general-purpose multi-voltage PSU

